1
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:29,290
[Live Forever]

2
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:33,000
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,760
¥800,000. Going once to Bidder No. 303.

4
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:36,700
As long as you're safe.

5
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,390
¥1,000,000. Going once to Bidder No. 250.

6
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:27,540
People are actually fighting over
such an unknown thing.

7
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:28,740
I think

8
00:02:28,770 --> 00:02:29,770
these two people

9
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,630
must have some personal grudge.

10
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:32,680
Exactly.

11
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,280
Boss.

12
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,880
Boss, please be rational.

13
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,710
Bidder No. 303, ¥2,000,000.

14
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:40,860
I…

15
00:02:40,890 --> 00:02:43,450
Bidder No. 250, ¥2,500,000.

16
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:51,590
Bidder No. 303, ¥3,000,000.

17
00:02:52,030 --> 00:02:54,750
Bidder No. 250, ¥3,500,000.

18
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,710
Bidder No. 303, ¥4,000,000.

19
00:02:56,950 --> 00:02:59,300
Bidder No. 250, ¥4,500,000.

20
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:00,760
¥5,000,000.

21
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:04,120
Sorry, sir.

22
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:06,370
This painting is priceless to me.

23
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:08,570
But if you really like it,

24
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:11,260
you can come to my place
and admire it anytime.

25
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:12,730
Let's just call it making friends.

26
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:13,540
¥8,000,000.

27
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:16,720
Sir,

28
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:17,530
I'm sorry.

29
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,850
You might not know me very well.

30
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,170
Anything I love,

31
00:03:21,590 --> 00:03:24,790
I don't like to leave it
at someone else's place to admire.

32
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:28,180
And I especially don't like it
being admired by others.

33
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:30,970
Okay.

34
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:34,740
I'm really sorry, everyone.

35
00:03:34,990 --> 00:03:36,720
Due to special circumstances,

36
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:39,310
the collector has suspended the auction.

37
00:03:39,490 --> 00:03:40,390
The auction for this item

38
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:41,590
ends here.

39
00:03:41,610 --> 00:03:42,340
That's not how it's done.

40
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:43,340
Apologies again.

41
00:03:44,190 --> 00:03:45,260
How unruly.

42
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:46,520
The hammer falls, the deal is done.

43
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,350
That's the rule of the auction house.

44
00:03:48,350 --> 00:03:49,280
What do you mean?

45
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,920
I'm really sorry, sir.

46
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:53,550
We are also communicating
with the collector.

47
00:03:53,550 --> 00:03:54,710
If there's any further news,

48
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:56,510
we will notify you immediately.

49
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,530
Sorry.

50
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:05,570
Ning Changyue.

51
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:07,430
You were the one who brought Yu Tu back,

52
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:08,580
but now you don't even care.

53
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:10,640
She's getting mud all over the house.

54
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,950
Lift your feet.

55
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,360
All you do is watch short dramas all day.

56
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:24,270
I wonder when you'll remember

57
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:25,530
how to break the vow
to live forever together.

58
00:04:25,530 --> 00:04:27,120
Move your big butt!

59
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,160
Since you are the only one,
of course I cherish you.

60
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,190
Unlike others,

61
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:33,620
you are now…

62
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:41,409
-Give it to me!
-No.

63
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:42,680
Give it to me!

64
00:04:42,730 --> 00:04:43,330
No!

65
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,820
You are now a member of the Censorate,

66
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,620
working under the Crown Prince.

67
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:53,060
Osmanthus-themed Painting
Special Exhibition.

68
00:04:54,409 --> 00:04:56,020
Autumn Art Gallery.

69
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:57,980
I didn't expect anyone to be

70
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,130
as obsessed with that painting as I am.

71
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,290
I don't know why either.

72
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,920
The very first moment I saw that painting,

73
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,040
I just really liked it
and wanted to own it.

74
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,440
Since you like it so much,

75
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,880
I want to get it even more.

76
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:16,120
Usually, when people hear
someone really likes something,

77
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,160
shouldn't they instinctively

78
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,950
want to let the other person have it?

79
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:20,070
I'm a businessman.

80
00:05:20,510 --> 00:05:21,840
I only care about value.

81
00:05:22,310 --> 00:05:23,360
After I get it,

82
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,920
you'll buy it at any price,

83
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:26,040
won't you?

84
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,790
Nice to meet you.

85
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:32,400
Let's make friends.

86
00:05:33,970 --> 00:05:35,030
My name is Lin Huai.

87
00:05:37,950 --> 00:05:40,280
You went to this Autumn Art Gallery today?

88
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,930
What is an art gallery?

89
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,480
Ning Changyue.

90
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,290
Ning Changyue.

91
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,490
He went out.

92
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:51,760
Went out?

93
00:05:52,270 --> 00:05:53,270
Where did he go?

94
00:05:54,159 --> 00:05:54,890
I don't know.

95
00:05:58,570 --> 00:06:00,270
This is our first time meeting each other.

96
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:01,530
We're not close enough

97
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:03,140
to be considered friends.

98
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:15,000
Sorry, the number you've dialed
is temporarily unavailable.

99
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:20,300
Aren't you going to wait
for Ning Changyue to come back?

100
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,120
Are you going by yourself?

101
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:26,210
What if Ning Changyue
makes some progress today?

102
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:27,870
Women

103
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:30,900
have to rely on themselves
at critical moments.

104
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:32,220
Hello.

105
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:37,640
Of course.

106
00:06:37,659 --> 00:06:39,990
It's an honor for us at
Autumn Art Gallery.

107
00:06:43,190 --> 00:06:43,720
Okay.

108
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,190
I'll go back now.

109
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,850
Autumn Art Gallery.

110
00:07:07,810 --> 00:07:09,470
Why does it sound so familiar?

111
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:20,830
Sorry.

112
00:07:21,310 --> 00:07:22,630
Our gallery is a private gallery

113
00:07:22,630 --> 00:07:24,110
that collects works
of niche anonymous painters.

114
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,640
It's not open to the public.

115
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:29,620
I'm sorry.

116
00:07:29,690 --> 00:07:30,490
My apologies.

117
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,920
Help me check all the exhibitions
about osmanthus trees.

118
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,400
Yes.

119
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:56,800
Paintings, calligraphy, vessels,
and clothing patterns

120
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:57,780
with osmanthus tree elements.

121
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:58,740
Any kind.

122
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,960
I'll call you back later.

123
00:08:10,230 --> 00:08:12,600
Did you draw this?

124
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:15,190
Yes. Thank you.

125
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:19,360
Your drawing is beautiful.

126
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:24,800
Many people think it's weird
that I like drawing trees.

127
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:26,930
If you like it, it's yours.

128
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:30,860
There was love in your heart
when you drew it.

129
00:08:34,390 --> 00:08:35,270
Look.

130
00:08:35,549 --> 00:08:36,480
All the branches

131
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:39,309
of this tree
are desperately growing upward,

132
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,030
as if they could touch something

133
00:08:41,030 --> 00:08:42,830
as long as they grow high enough.

134
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:44,850
It shows there's an obsession

135
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,480
in your heart.

136
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:52,160
Sorry, it's force of habit.

137
00:08:53,110 --> 00:08:54,060
My name is Xie He,

138
00:08:54,190 --> 00:08:55,260
a clinical psychologist

139
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:56,290
at Hexin Psychological Clinic.

140
00:08:55,950 --> 00:08:56,330
[Xie He]

141
00:09:01,550 --> 00:09:02,470
Song Yiqiu.

142
00:09:03,390 --> 00:09:04,840
Song Yiqiu.

143
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:07,570
Nice to meet you.

144
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:17,750
Why is this guy here again in this life?

145
00:09:18,730 --> 00:09:20,260
Song Yiqiu saved him again.

146
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:20,940
Autumn…

147
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:24,030
Autumn…

148
00:09:24,050 --> 00:09:25,290
Lingering ghost.

149
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:26,560
Autumn Moon…

150
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,240
Lingering ghost.

151
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,600
Lingering ghost.

152
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:32,270
Autumn…

153
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:34,080
In this life,

154
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:36,200
I must never let him meet Song Yiqiu.

155
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:37,870
Autumn…

156
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:40,810
-Lingering ghost.
-What do you mean?

157
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,150
Nothing.

158
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:52,630
Stop.

159
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,120
You…

160
00:09:55,510 --> 00:09:56,840
Today,

161
00:09:58,030 --> 00:09:58,870
where did you go?

162
00:09:58,870 --> 00:09:59,670
Me?

163
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:02,870
To an auction.

164
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:04,080
An auction?

165
00:10:04,510 --> 00:10:05,910
It was popular hundreds of years ago.

166
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:07,570
Why do you still want to go now?

167
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:09,070
Then what did you buy?

168
00:10:09,630 --> 00:10:10,760
-I didn't…
-Autumn…

169
00:10:11,630 --> 00:10:12,720
I didn't buy anything.

170
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:14,360
I just looked around.

171
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,400
You dressed up so nicely.

172
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,330
Where did you go?

173
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Don't mention it.

174
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,670
I got nothing.

175
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,840
"Autumn Moon in the Forest."

176
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,670
Did you find…

177
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,870
"Autumn Moon in the Forest"?

178
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:44,660
Song Yiqiu.

179
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,480
Deal with him.

180
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,200
"Autumn Moon in the Forest"

181
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,730
might be the sacred painting
that seals time?

182
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,670
Such important news.

183
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,440
Why didn't you tell me?

184
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:57,480
Ning Changyue.

185
00:10:58,030 --> 00:10:59,790
I'm talking to you.

186
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:02,840
Why didn't you take me with you?

187
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,960
It's not that I didn't want to
take you with me.

188
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:04,720
I wasn't even sure myself

189
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:06,390
if this was reliable.

190
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:11,670
I think you're just feeling guilty.

191
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:14,030
What, was there someone I shouldn't see?

192
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:23,520
You knew it?

193
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:31,840
Was it your Miss Liu or Miss Wang?

194
00:11:31,910 --> 00:11:33,440
But don't worry.

195
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,790
I know everything.

196
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:36,030
I don't care.

197
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:37,830
You don't have to hide it from me.

198
00:11:38,390 --> 00:11:39,000
Yeah.

199
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:42,870
The auction. The antique shop.
The top ten beauties were all there.

200
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:44,150
Of course I couldn't let you go.

201
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:46,360
And in the end, that painting went unsold.

202
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,960
The scroll was only half unrolled.

203
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,420
It would have been
a waste of time if you went.

204
00:11:50,770 --> 00:11:53,050
Could it be because you

205
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:55,320
have too much bad luck?

206
00:11:55,670 --> 00:11:57,310
If it were me,

207
00:11:57,390 --> 00:11:59,240
since I have better luck than you,

208
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,240
I definitely would have won the bid.

209
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:03,320
If you had gone,

210
00:12:03,790 --> 00:12:05,510
someone else would have had the good luck.

211
00:12:05,510 --> 00:12:06,550
What did you say?

212
00:12:06,910 --> 00:12:09,320
I'm talking to you, Ning Changyue!

213
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:11,050
Alright, stop talking.

214
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,330
Let me think about it

215
00:12:12,910 --> 00:12:15,440
and try to reconstruct it
for you from memory.

216
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,750
We weren't allowed to take photos
of the auction items.

217
00:12:17,750 --> 00:12:18,630
I only took one look,

218
00:12:18,630 --> 00:12:21,430
so I might not be able to
reconstruct it perfectly.

219
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,900
Prepare the brush and ink.

220
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,840
Me?

221
00:12:29,870 --> 00:12:30,960
Who else?

222
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,360
Didn't you want to see the painting?

223
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,150
You haven't seen it,

224
00:12:34,150 --> 00:12:35,550
so you can only rely on me.

225
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,600
Alright.

226
00:12:38,870 --> 00:12:39,840
Brush.

227
00:12:47,150 --> 00:12:47,790
Ink.

228
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,720
Be serious.

229
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:01,060
This is delicate work.

230
00:13:01,090 --> 00:13:02,470
Even a slight mistake will prevent you

231
00:13:02,470 --> 00:13:05,020
from reproducing the elegance
of "Autumn Moon in the Forest."

232
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:06,660
Are you going to draw or not?

233
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,440
Mountains.

234
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,160
A full moon.

235
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,240
What else?

236
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,400
Why did you stop drawing?

237
00:13:52,590 --> 00:13:53,960
This tree crown…

238
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,580
I don't really know how to draw it.

239
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:00,790
Then do you still remember

240
00:14:00,790 --> 00:14:02,590
what this tree crown looks like?

241
00:14:04,830 --> 00:14:06,370
It has quite thick foliage.

242
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:09,290
And the branches stretch out
in all directions,

243
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:12,420
forming a huge umbrella shape.

244
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:18,240
Didn't I teach you
during the Southern Qin period?

245
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:01,640
Focus.

246
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:26,270
You can't even draw
such a simple tree crown?

247
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,920
This tree crown…

248
00:15:54,550 --> 00:15:55,390
This tree crown

249
00:15:55,390 --> 00:15:56,790
is very tree crown-like.

250
00:15:58,030 --> 00:15:59,750
I'll go call Yu Tu over here.

251
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:02,870
She should know

252
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:04,680
about the tree, right?

253
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,400
What do you mean
by "very tree crown-like"?

254
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,700
What are you thinking about, Song Yiqiu?

255
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,510
You two are no longer

256
00:16:52,510 --> 00:16:55,510
the Song Yiqiu and Ning Changyue
from 3,000 years ago.

257
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,440
Did you forget?

258
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,349
It's so late.

259
00:17:06,109 --> 00:17:06,930
Who is it?

260
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,069
You're…

261
00:17:20,069 --> 00:17:23,200
Is this Mr. Ning's house?

262
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:26,089
No.

263
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:32,720
I got the wrong place?

264
00:17:34,590 --> 00:17:35,640
No.

265
00:17:36,070 --> 00:17:37,640
But he's a tenant,

266
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:39,510
and I'm the landlord.

267
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:46,680
Have some water.

268
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:48,550
Thank you.

269
00:17:52,270 --> 00:17:55,000
I didn't expect someone
as successful as Mr. Ning

270
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:56,200
to still be…

271
00:17:56,880 --> 00:18:00,140
-Fifteen. Fifteen. Fifteen.
-Fifteen. Fifteen. Twenty.

272
00:18:00,550 --> 00:18:02,150
Sharing a place with others.

273
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,940
Save when you can, spend when you should.

274
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,820
Manager Qing Yuan,
you came to see me so late.

275
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:20,220
Is something the matter?

276
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:22,880
I came here specifically to apologize.

277
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:25,890
Today, the owner
canceled the auction halfway through,

278
00:18:25,890 --> 00:18:28,310
so you couldn't win the bid
on "Autumn Moon in the Forest."

279
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:29,240
I'm sorry.

280
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,990
Now, this painting
is in the Autumn Art Gallery.

281
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:34,160
Please look.

